<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.10.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02261</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.10.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0b1a5851-9874-46bb-ad75-7ef0ecfc1ac3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <exercise id="_5f65cc8d-fbf0-4264-985d-80ccbb2ee4f4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">For questions 1 – 4, find the factored form of the quadratic expression.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">\(3x^2+ 16x + 5\)</para>
          <para id="para-00004">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00005">\((3x − 5)(x − 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00006">\((3x + 1)(x - 5)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00007">\((3x − 1)(x − 5)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00008">\((3x + 1)(x + 5)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is \((3x + 1)(x + 5)\) .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_885451ea-6a0d-43bb-a2e2-66dcec6ebf4d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00011">\(2x^2+ 11x − 6\)</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00013">\((2x + 6)(x − 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00014">\((2x − 6)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00015">\((2x − 1)(x + 6)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00016">\((2x + 1)(x − 6)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is \((2x − 1)(x + 6)\) .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_71fed853-ac3a-4c2b-acca-01fd838d8b32" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00019">\(4x^2− 13x + 3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00020">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00021">\((4x − 1)(x − 3)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00022">\((4x + 3)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00023">\((4x − 3)(x − 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00024">\((4x + 1)(x + 3)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00025">Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00026">The correct answer is \((4x − 1)(x − 3)\) .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_7bd97612-9bcd-4e35-b7a2-71ad543b985b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00027">\(2x^2−3x −2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00028">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00029">\((2x + 1)(x − 2)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00030">\((2x + 2)(x − 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00031">\((2x − 2)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00032">\((2x − 1)(x + 2)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is \((2x + 1)(x − 2)\) .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_0a46316d-2d16-4e78-a061-e7272eae6ee9" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00035">The height, in meters, of a baseball being hit is modeled by the function \(h(x) = -2x^2+ 12x + 3\) where \(x\) is the number of seconds since being hit. Approximately how many seconds pass before the baseball lands on the ground? Use graphing technology if needed.</para>
          <para id="para-00036">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00037">4.38 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00038">6.24 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00039">7.26 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00040">7.56 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00041">Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00042">The correct answer is 6.24 seconds .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_06fd0036-d5b6-4199-96e0-4ecf8c671b62" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00043">The height, in meters, of a roller coaster is modeled by the function \(h(x) = -2x^2 + 20x + 5\) where \(x\) is the number of seconds after starting. Approximately how many seconds pass before the roller coaster reaches the ground? Use graphing technology if needed.</para>
          <para id="para-00044">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00045">5.221 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00046">7.963 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00047">8.365 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00048">10.244 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00049">Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00050">The correct answer is 10.244 seconds .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="b796bb7a-1f2a-422c-995b-d498e03b9a34" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00051">For questions 7 – 10, find the factored form of the quadratic expression.</para>
          <para id="para-00052">\(3x^2 + 2x − 5\)</para>
          <para id="para-00053">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00054">\((3x + 5)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00055">\((x + 5)(3x − 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00056">\((3x + 5)(x − 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00057">\((3x − 5)(x + 1)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00058">Try again. Revisit activities 8.10.2 and 8.10.5.</para>
          <para id="para-00059">The correct answer is \((3x + 5)(x − 1)\) .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="c7c95a68-b05d-4b64-84d7-e872ef7f7687" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00060">\(4x^2+ 4x − 15\)</para>
          <para id="para-00061">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00062">\((4x − 3)(x + 5)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00063">\((2x − 3)(2x + 5)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00064">\((4x + 3)(x − 5)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00065">\((2x + 3)(2x − 5)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00066">Try again. Revisit activities 8.10.2 and 8.10.5.</para>
          <para id="para-00067">The correct answer is \((2x − 3)(2x + 5)\) .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_9523d2c9-fddb-4b93-bb3e-1e5f0ad6a8df" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00068">\(5x^2− 39x − 8\)</para>
          <para id="para-00069">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00070">\((5x − 1)(x + 8)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00071">\((5x + 8)(x − 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00072">\((5x − 8)(x + 1)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00073">\((5x + 1)(x − 8)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00074">Try again. Revisit activities 8.10.2 and 8.10.5.</para>
          <para id="para-00075">The correct answer is \((5x + 1)(x − 8)\) .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d36f22e4-b400-4555-8a81-111a108f6e0b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00076">\(6x^2+ 53x − 9\)</para>
          <para id="para-00077">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00078">\((6x − 1)(x + 9)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00079">\((3x − 1)(2x + 9)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00080">\((2x − 1)(3x + 9)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00081">\((6x + 1)(x − 9)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00082">Try again. Revisit activities 8.10.2 and 8.10.5.</para>
          <para id="para-00083">The correct answer is \((6x − 1)(x + 9)\) .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
